---
pre-compare: sort
---
from_file env("TENZIR_INPUT") {
  read_json
}
// The same stored-shape chain with four post-stamp mutations applied
// in the store — the verification lane's threat model. (1) The a1
// record was DELETED: a2 is now the first record of the walk yet still
// references a predecessor the walk never sees — the rolling-window
// tolerance (windowed=true) treats that as the window edge, not a
// break; in the unwindowed investigations walk the same shape is the
// chain_head_missing deletion finding. (2) a2's unmapped.response_code
// was edited after stamping with its attestation left stale: the
// per-record fingerprint recompute must flag it — proving the
// fingerprint check runs even at the window edge. (3) The auth record
// was DELETED: audit-b's prev_event no longer references its immediate
// walked predecessor, and the walk must flag the broken link. (4)
// audit-b's INTACT link must flag the auth deletion. (4) The
// finding record's chain-link attestation (attestation_list[1]) was
// stripped: a mid-chain record without its link is the documented
// restart shape — NOT a break (the un-hashed link carries no
// fingerprint to recompute; its integrity is enforced by the adjacency
// check that (3) just proved on audit-b). Expected: the summary line
// plus two findings — fingerprint_mismatch on a2 and
// chain_link_mismatch on audit-b.
fork {
  summarize records_checked = count()
  to_stdout { write_json }
}
homelab::record_integrity::verify product="homelab-detection",
  title="Detection record chain break",
  uid_prefix="detection",
  scope_word="chain",
  windowed=true,
  link="stream"
// Findings only reach here (the walk drops intact records); pin the
// finding time for the baseline — the operator stamps now() live.
time = 2026-10-17T11:30:00Z
